WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
The craftsmen of Shang could make exquisite bronze vessels.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:07.934
Their technology was very advanced for its time.

00:00:08.284 --> 00:00:12.628
The craftsmen first made the molds, then carefully carved in the patterns.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:16.794
Every single vessel required the effort of many people.

00:00:17.144 --> 00:00:22.832
The craftsmen mixed copper and tin, melting them into glowing liquid bronze.

00:00:23.182 --> 00:00:28.534
The bronze slowly flowed into the molds, taking the shape of the vessels.

00:00:28.884 --> 00:00:32.604
Once it had cooled, a bronze vessel was complete.

00:00:32.954 --> 00:00:38.474
The huge ding cauldrons and fine wine vessels gleamed brightly.

00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:41.992
Many bronze vessels were used during ritual ceremonies.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:45.630
They also represented the status and power of the nobility.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.276
Today, museums preserve many bronze vessels from the Shang.

00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:54.874
They let us see the superb technology and art of the ancients.

